# CMS wiring — never break the content layer

When editing marketing sections, homepage copy, CTAs, or navigation, preserve CMS-driven values. Visual and layout refactors are fine; disconnecting Sanity is not.

## Golden rule

Never remove or bypass CMS variables while hardcoding replacement copy in components. If copy or links are editable in Sanity Studio, the component must still read them.

## Two content sources

| Source | Document | Use for |
|--------|----------|---------|
| Site-wide | `siteSettings` | Nav, footer, `headerCta`, `sharedLinks` |
| Page-specific | `homepageContent` (page singletons) | Section headings, body copy, arrays for that page |

PageLayout forwards `siteSettings` to Header/Footer only. Page routes fetch their own content and pass props into sections.

## Before merging section redesigns

1. Props still used — `{headerCta.label}`, `data?.steps`, not string literals when CMS fields exist
2. Parent still passes props from `sanityFetch`
3. Schema, GROQ query, types, and component props stay in sync
4. Shared URLs live in `siteSettings.sharedLinks`, not scattered in components
5. `headerCta` renders `{headerCta.label}` and `{headerCta.href}` when present

## Hardcoding is allowed only as fallbacks

```tsx
const steps = data?.steps?.length ? data.steps : DEFAULT_STEPS;
const label = meetingLabel ?? "Book a 30 min call";
```

## New homepage sections

Require: Sanity schema → GROQ query → TypeScript type → section `data` prop → page route → Studio seed. Archive replaced sections under `src/components/archived/`; do not drop queries/fields until replacements are wired.

## Anti-patterns

- `{headerCta && ...}` with hardcoded label/href inside
- `data?: SolutionData` accepted but ignored in the component
- Hardcoding meeting labels in many files instead of `sharedLinks.meetingLabel`
- Product URLs inline when they belong in `sharedLinks`
